WEBVTT

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:14.560
The first years of a young animal's life are the most crucial.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.680
So, if they grow up without their mothers, these animals are going to need help.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.120
Good morning!

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:22.600
Hello, darling.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:29.240
We're going to meet baby animals whose only hope of survival lies with some very dedicated people...

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.360
What a clever girl.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:37.840
..And find out what it takes to get them back into the wild.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:46.680
This is about salvation for some little guys who've been through hell, who've been through trauma, who deserve a second chance.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:55.640
'I'm biologist Patrick Aryee' and I'm in Central America, home to exotic and rare wildlife.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.320
'Here, I'll be visiting centres where the wildlife 'gets incredible specialist care.'

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.680
That is remarkable!

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:12.080
'And I'm zoologist Lucy Cooke' and I'm in southern Africa, home to some of the most iconic animals in the world.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:17.280
'I'll be helping out at rescue centres 'devoted to rehabilitation and release.'

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:23.720
You're going to become a wild cheetah one day, aren't you, if you carry on being this good.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:35.440
'In this programme, I'll be meeting Manji, the baby rhino... '..who after a traumatic start to life 'now has to learn the skills he needs 'to return to the African savanna.'

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.560
Look at these guys!

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.000
They are ready to be wild rhinos.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:50.080
'And I'll be helping Mandi, the orphaned tapir... '..discover her wilder side... '..so she can be reintroduced to her own kind.'

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.080
Oh, my God.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:56.160
Mandi.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.400
Join us as we follow these miracle orphans.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.640
Through their most crucial moments.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:10.160
On their long journeys back to the wild.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:22.360
South Africa... ..home to some of the most loved and recognisable animals on the planet.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:31.760
But pressures are mounting on the wildlife here and many species are now under threat.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.760
None more high-profile than the African white rhino.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:49.120
These extraordinary ancient beasts have roamed our earth for 50 million years but due to a recent surge in poaching, there are only 20,000 left in the wild.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:57.120
Experts believe that they could completely disappear from the wild in the next five years, which means that every animal counts.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.880
This is four-month old Manji...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.800
There you go, my boy.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:09.560
..An orphaned baby white rhino that lives here at Care For Wild Africa...

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.680
Oh!

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.400
It's a nice, wonderful morning.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.920
Did you sleep well, my boy?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.440
Did you sleep well?

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:21.920
..A rescue centre founded by Petronel Nieuwoudt.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:32.320
She has over 20 years' experience working with wildlife and is surrogate mum to over 20 rhinos.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.280
Hello, my girl, you're so big and so strong!

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.120
Look at that!

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:42.080
Petronel's rhinos are all at different stages of rehabilitation.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:52.280
Some are large enough to roam free in a wild reserve... ..but rescued babies need care around the clock.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.800
Happy baby!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.360
And baby Manji is her biggest challenge yet.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.920
'Manji means place of the stars.'

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.560
And he's a star, he's a star in my life.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:09.840
He is the youngest rhino that Petronel has ever rescued.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:13.800
OK, drips in first, drips in first.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:23.079
At just two days old, his mother was killed by poachers for her horn... ..and he too was attacked with a machete, receiving near-fatal head injuries.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:30.720
In every rescue, the first 48 hours are crucial.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.880
Petronel didn't leave Manji's side.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:40.080
He was so small and so skinny, the blood loss was immense and I called everyone I know.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.560
I just know, "Hey, we're going to save this one."

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:48.320
And after intense medical treatment, doctors managed to save him.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:55.400
Manji is the survivor of survivors, he's a brilliant little one.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:05:00.880
I'm very, very proud of him and I love him, I love him to bits.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:10.680
Manji now needs to learn how to be a wild rhino and Petronel is determined that he and all her orphans return to where they belong.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:17.240
There was never a choice for me in looking after these giants.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:24.160
It's a journey, it's a lifelong commitment.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.280
I want them to be free, I want them to be in the wild.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:32.960
On average, three rhinos a day are poached for their horns.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.880
'Unsurprisingly, Petronel will take on any orphan that needs her help.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:45.760
'The first stage of a rhino's rehabilitation is crucial 'and she wants to show me where their recovery begins.'

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.480
So, this is the intensive care unit?

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:46.720
Yeah.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:55.760
This is where we have the babies, smaller babies or the animals that just came in after their rescue.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:06:01.000
'In this intensive care unit, the most important thing 'is making sure orphans get the right nutrition.'

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.240
Hello!

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.520
Hello.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.600
There we go!

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:12.440
'And nothing comes between a hungry rhino and its bottle.'

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.600
Hello, is that good?

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.800
So tiny!

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:24.760
Wow, they drank that so fast and that's just one of seven bottles that they drink every day.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:32.240
But then these guys need to drink between 10 and 15% of their body weight every day, so it's a lot of milk.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:41.520
White rhinos are highly social mammals and babies depend on their mothers for the first three years.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.160
Come sit down.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:42.960
There we go, there we go.

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:54.120
Having raised so many orphans, Petronel has a deep understanding of their emotions.

00:06:53.320 --> 00:07:01.000
They are these giant, wonderful creatures and to build the trust with these guys is of utmost importance.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:07.920
Really softly with a lot of emotion to make them feel safe, to make them feel that we look after their needs.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:12.800
What's the most important part of the process of rehabilitation for Manji?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.240
We want to release him back into the wild.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:22.040
They are herd animals, they like to socialise and they play.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.360
If I see him doing well in those stages, I know he will do well outside there.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:25.280
In order to be a wild rhino, he's got to join the herd basically for survival?

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:30.160
Absolutely.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.680
Yeah.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:30.800
Absolutely so, yeah.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:37.080
Over the next few weeks, Manji needs to learn how to fend for himself.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.240
His whole world is about to change.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:52.040
His next step is to leave this intensive care unit - the only place he's known for the last four months - and with these other orphans, move to a bigger space.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:59.760
There, he'll practise the skills he'll need to prepare him for the wild.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.960
Over 7,500 miles away is Costa Rica.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.560
This meeting place of the Americas boasts a wealth of natural habitats.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:13.400
It's a small country, a quarter of the size of the UK.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:26.760
Bursting with wildlife, it's home to half a million species... ..making it one of the most biodiverse places on earth.

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:38.559
But with a growing human population, many of the extraordinary animals that live here are now under threat.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.120
I'm on my way to a very special wildlife sanctuary on the Pacific coast of Costa Rica.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:52.120
Now, it's in a really remote location and for good reason too, because the animals that it cares for are some of the most exotic and endangered in all of Central America.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:59.080
I'm heading to the Macaw Sanctuary, run by Rodolfo Orozco Vega.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:11.040
In his 15 years here, he's seen it expand and he now rescues and cares for many of Costa Rica's rarest animals, including majestic jaguars and these vocal characters.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:16.600
What you can hear is the sound of great green macaws, what fabulous animals.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:21.800
There are only 300 or so left in Costa Rica.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:27.280
And they aren't the only endangered animals that he's protecting.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.800
This is Mandi.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:38.440
She's a Baird's tapir.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:44.440
These herbivores are known to be shy and timid creatures.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:58.000
Related to horses and rhinos, they're able to use their nose like a hand to pull leaves from branches and pick up food that's dropped to the ground.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:58.600
So, Rodolfo, this is...

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:01.080
This is Mandi.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.960
..The lovely Mandi.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.360
Hello, Mandi.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:09.560
This is the first time I've met a tapir.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.800
There you go, Mandi.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:12.240
She's lovely.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:13.840
I love how she's just resting on me.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.400
She seems very relaxed, very happy, content and quite tranquil.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:22.520
And you can see from Mandi's face, whilst I'm feeding her, her eyes are completely closed.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:27.480
'Mandi is an orphan.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:33.920
'She was rescued from poachers at just four weeks old.'

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:42.360
'She was found tied up in a local village 'and was close to starvation.'

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.600
How big was she when she first came to the centre?

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:56.760
She was very little, very sick, sad and covered with scratches all over her body, even a scar in her neck because she was tied up by people.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:01.480
So, the reason why she was so scarred and bruised was because of humans?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.880
Yeah, exactly.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:05.480
Humans were trying to eat Mandi, that simple.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:14.160
Hunters killed the mother and they take the baby to their houses to, you know, to grow up and to eat it later.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:27.120
'Tapirs are a protected species in Costa Rica 'but being hunted and eaten by humans 'is still one of the main threats they're facing.'

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:37.120
Don't you find it surprising that, considering there are only 5,000 of these tapirs left in the wild, that people are still hunting them?

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:42.960
Yeah, it is really surprising because that's why we are trying to save her.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:47.680
We have to do whatever we can to keep her safe and healthy.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.360
That's my role here, being Mandi's mum.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:12:03.840
In the wild, baby tapirs are camouflaged with stripes until around three months old and they're reliant on their mothers for milk and protection.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.960
Mandi is five months old, how do you think she's doing now?

00:12:06.280 --> 00:12:09.320
She's doing very well.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:17.880
She's now acting more like a tapir instead of being, you know, close to humans and begging for human company.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.320
Now, she's more independent, she's doing very well.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.560
And with her new-found confidence, Mandi is starting to become a bit of a handful.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:31.720
As if on cue!

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:40.840
It's interesting seeing Mandi who, you know, seemed like a very relaxed creature... ..but now she's getting a lot more active.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:44.680
That milk's finished and she wants to play.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:54.400
And her method of playing is head-butting, which actually can be quite painful considering how big she is.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:59.480
'Baby tapirs use playtime to learn survival skills.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:04.440
'It's not just humans that want to eat them.

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:07.080
'In the wild, they have to avoid being eaten by predators.'

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:16.840
Now, as much as she is the largest land mammal in Central America and South America, she does have predators and one of those predators is a jaguar.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.240
Now, there are several things that tapirs have to their advantage.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:25.520
One is their massive size and also they have a thick hide, especially around the neck.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:29.320
That is where the jaguar is going to try and target.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:33.920
So, all this activity, all this play, is really important for her to learn how to be a wild tapir.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:43.800
'This defensive play also signals that Mandi is ready 'for the next stage in her rehabilitation.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.480
She's showing us who's boss, that's for sure.

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:49.200
Yeah.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:53.720
I'm trying to stay light on my feet right now.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:14:00.960
'Rodolfo's plan is to introduce her gradually 'to two other rescued tapirs in the sanctuary.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:04.000
'The challenge for Mandi now is to be accepted by her own kind.'

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:19.600
Over 7,500 miles away, I'm in South Africa 'helping Manji, the baby rhino.'

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:34.640
This intensive care unit has been instrumental in helping Manji overcome the trauma of his past, but it's time for him to move on and discover the world beyond these four walls.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:41.240
Petronel's sanctuary is set in nearly 5,000 hectares of African bushveld.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:50.400
And Manji is moving to a purpose-built enclosure known as a boma.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.600
But he won't be moving alone.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:59.440
Since arriving here, he's formed a very strong bond with two other rhinos who, like him, had a traumatic start in life.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:02.240
Mia and Venus.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:07.280
Do you want to pick me up?

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:15.280
Petronel has spent so much time nursing and caring for this trio, she knows all their character traits.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:22.480
If you look at the personalities just in this camp here, you could clearly see who is the cheeky one and the feisty one and that's Venus.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:25.760
She will protect these guys and be a real matriarch, you know, a real leader.

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:36.720
Mia is just such a softie, enjoy to be touched, very affectionate, where Manji, look at him playing there, brilliant boy, inquisitive.

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:42.760
Not too bothered about what the girls are up to at all.

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:53.160
Their new home is over 1km away and is ten times larger than their old one.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:16:04.120
It's situated on the edge of the wild reserve, where a herd of rhinos roam free.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:08.480
Petronel's dream is that Manji will soon join them.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:18.040
She has designed every element of the boma and is making a final check to ensure everything is in order.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.360
A last inspection.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.720
Now, that's good.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:18.920
And then one in that corner.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:27.560
With experience and other animals, you can put them through the rehabilitation process so much quicker.

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:33.840
So, for me it's quite important to make sure that this boma and their new home will be the best for them ever.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:40.560
It's like a palace, it's like a castle for a king, you know, and that's what I want for them.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.400
I think they will enjoy this immensely.

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:54.560
Manji and his herd, Venus and Mia, have all had traumatic pasts, so Petronel wants to make this journey as easy as possible.

00:16:53.760 --> 00:17:04.040
Having years of experience moving rhinos, her plan is to transport them across the sanctuary while they are under sedation.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.480
Jump, jump, jump, jump, jump.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:05.800
Jump, jump.

00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:06.240
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:06.560
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.680
Yeah.

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.440
See here.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.240
Now, our pulse ox is working, thank you.

00:17:10.359 --> 00:17:13.319
We're just making sure all the equipment is working fine.

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:17.640
You don't want to stand here and then the equipment is not doing what they're supposed to do.

00:17:18.319 --> 00:17:28.880
Giving anaesthetic to one young animal is worrying, but immobilising all three of them comes with even greater risks.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.200
Ja, it's a big day.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:37.800
Sitting with this headache just over my eyes here and it only lift when the animals are awake and happy and doing well and breathing fine again.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:46.440
With preparation complete, Manji is the first of his herd to be moved.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:54.200
And wildlife vet Dr Ferreira uses a pole syringe to inject him with a sedative.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:18:04.360
He's very used to be with Venus and Mia, so I can see it in his eyes as well the chemical... start working as well.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:10.360
Petronel uses a blindfold and earplugs to reduce the stress.

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:15.280
While he's under sedation, there's one other routine job to do.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:25.400
Rhino horn is made of keratin, a protein composed of dead cells, like human hair and nails.

00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:29.920
With no nerves or feeling in it, Petronel believes that keeping it short is a painless and vital way to stop Manji being poached.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:38.320
I don't want to put Manji's life in danger, so if they go out to the wild where everyone want them and they have their horn on, they're going to be killed.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:48.640
They are going to be poached and we will find more carcasses.

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:54.080
So if we can protect them, let's do everything in our power to protect them.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:19:04.880
Rhino horn is highly sought-after on the international black market, to be used in traditional Chinese medicine.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:11.000
It's the main reason that rhinos are killed in the wild.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.480
You see.

00:19:11.560 --> 00:19:14.400
One, two, three.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:14.680
Come to the front.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:28.200
With his horn trimmed, the team are confident that they have taken every precaution to protect him and he is on his way across the sanctuary to his new home.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:35.560
The vet team reverse the effects of the anaesthetic and Manji gets up quickly.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:36.960
You can clearly hear him sniffing.

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:43.360
Smelling everything in the new house.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:47.040
It looks like it smells very nice.

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:47.360
This is so great.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:52.880
We're going to get Venus now, ja, ja.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.400
And then the two of you can discuss this crazy new house.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:06.400
The preparation for Venus is a little bit different.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:06.720
We need everyone away and it must be very quiet with Venus.

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:13.320
She's a complete different animal than Manji.

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:20.160
If she picks up on any movement, her adrenaline is going to kick in and then we won't be able to work with her at all.

00:20:22.440 --> 00:20:27.600
If Venus becomes too stressed, the anaesthetic won't be as effective and she could injure herself or the team.

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:37.760
But with patience and the right conditions, Venus eventually goes to sleep.

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:49.640
And with her horn trimmed, she too is ready to be taken to her new home.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.680
Mia gets the same treatment and is not far behind.

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:01.480
It's an amazing feeling.

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:02.560
Look at this.

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:06.520
S Reunited, the herd begin to enjoy the boma's design features.

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:14.040
Already eating, already very interested, this is their new Jacuzzi mud bath.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:19.880
A mud bath is not something that Manji has ever experienced.

00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:23.440
And he isn't quite sure what to make of it.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.960
Manji doesn't know what this is.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:28.960
So, we have to definitely try and teach Manji the enjoyment of the water and the mud.

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:38.440
He's actually at the moment hiding away a little bit and scratching himself against the tyre.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:46.880
And that, for him, is what he knows.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:51.840
But herd leader Venus is keen to give the Jacuzzi mud bath a try.

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:52.680
Oh-ooh, dis so lekker.

