Rhinos rely heavily on their well-developed sense of smell and they use it in the wild to detect other animals from over a quarter of a mile away.

00:31:11.200 --> 00:31:13.120
This is a big, big, big step for them.

00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:19.360
This new space is packed full of new smells, and the unfamiliar triggers a defensive instinct.

00:31:20.040 --> 00:31:25.000
The way they're standing is also protecting each other.

00:31:24.120 --> 00:31:27.400
Very good behaviour for rhino.

00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:32.720
And there's Manji and Venus following me now.

00:31:34.360 --> 00:31:43.160
Manji's staying with Venus and they will just carry along and come more out and more out and test the waters more and more and more.

00:31:44.800 --> 00:31:53.520
With herd leader Venus at ease, Manji and Mia relax too.

00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:56.520
It's like a herd.

00:31:55.600 --> 00:31:56.800
Wow.

00:31:55.840 --> 00:31:59.400
It looks like they have been doing this forever.

00:31:58.440 --> 00:32:01.800
For me, that's so amazing, you know?

00:32:02.720 --> 00:32:03.880
They've been through hell.

